  "tekst": "\"Gas! GAS! Quick, boys! — An ecstasy of fumbling / […] Dim, through the misty panes and thick green light, / As under a green sea, I saw him drowning. / […] If in some smothering dreams you too could pace / Behind the wagon that we flung him in, / And watch the white eyes writhing in his face, / […] My friend, you would not tell with such high zest / To children ardent for some desperate glory, / The old Lie: Dulce et decorum est / Pro patria mori.\"",
  "caption": "W. Owen, 'Dulce et Decorum Est', geschreven in Craiglockhart Hospital (Schotland), oktober 1917. Postuum gepubliceerd in Poems by Wilfred Owen (Londen, Chatto & Windus, 1920).",
